@startsalt
' Screen: Run Detail (Most Important Screen)
' Related user stories:
'   US-30: As a QA engineer, I want to see the full conversation replay of a run
'   US-31: As a QA engineer, I want to see per-turn scores and freeball annotations
'   US-32: As a QA engineer, I want to cancel, export, or re-score a run from its detail page
'   US-33: As a QA engineer, I want to see overall pass/warn/fail verdict prominently

{
  ' Breadcrumb + header
  <i>Runs /</i> <b>Run #R-2847</b>
  ==
  ' Run identity row
  {
    <b>checkout-flow v3</b>  →  <b>gpt-4o v2</b>  ·  Persona: <b>hostile-user</b>
    | " " | Status: <color:blue><b>RUNNING</b></color>
    | Started: <b>2m ago</b>  ·  Cost: <b>$0.31</b> / $5.00 cap
  }
  ==
  ' Verdict banner (prominent — shows on completion, placeholder while running)
  {+
    " " | <i>Verdict will appear here upon completion</i>
    " "
    <i>Run in progress... 7 / 12 nodes complete</i>
    " "
  }
  --
  ' Score summary card
  {
    <b>Score Summary</b>
    {
      Overall: <b>0.87</b> | Pass: <color:green><b>4</b></color> | Warn: <color:orange><b>1</b></color> | Fail: <color:red><b>0</b></color> | Freeball: <b>2</b>
    }
  }
  ==
  ' Tabs
  {/ <b>Conversation</b> | Steps | Scores }
  ==
  ' Conversation tab content
  <b>Conversation Timeline</b>  <i>hostile-user persona · 4 turns shown</i>
  --
  ' Turn 1: authored user node
  {+
    <b>USER</b>  <i>(authored node · turn 1)</i>
    "I want to return my order #45892. It arrived damaged."
  }
  --
  ' Turn 2: agent response with score chip
  {+
    <b>AGENT</b>  <i>(turn 2)</i>                                        score: <color:green>[0.92]</color>
    "I'd be happy to help with your return for order #45892."
    "I'm sorry to hear it arrived damaged. Let me pull up your"
    "order details and get this sorted for you right away."
    --
    <i>Expectations: greeting ✓ · empathy ✓ · order_lookup called ✓</i>
  }
  --
  ' Turn 3: freeball user node (orange tint)
  {+
    <color:darkorange><b>USER</b>  <i>(freeball node · turn 3 · depth 1)</i></color>
    <color:darkorange>"Actually, what IS your refund policy anyway?"</color>
    <color:darkorange><i>⚡ Freeball: user deviated from authored script path</i></color>
  }
  --
  ' Turn 4: agent response with lower score
  {+
    <b>AGENT</b>  <i>(turn 4)</i>                                        score: <color:orange>[0.78]</color>
    "Our refund policy allows returns within 30 days of delivery"
    "for most items. Damaged items are eligible for a full refund"
    "or replacement at no cost to you."
    --
    <i>Expectations: policy_accuracy ✓ · damaged_item_path △ (partial)</i>
  }
  --
  <i>... 3 more turns · run in progress ...</i>
  ==
  ' Action bar
  {
    [ Cancel Run ] | [ Export JSON ] | [ Re-score... ] | " " | [ ← Back to Runs ]
  }
}
@endsalt
